WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.580
In any school, it's vital that kids feel
safe and valued. These are among the

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:15.020
laudable goals of social and emotional
learning, or SEL. But SEL advocates need

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:20.340
to keep in mind some crucial cautions.
Here are two: One, promoting student safety

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:25.320
should not turn into an excuse to push
an agenda. Some SEL proponents seem

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.070
particularly taken with "restorative
justice" and tend to overstate the

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:34.800
evidence that it "works." Students should
feel safe and valued, and strategies to

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:40.559
make that happen should be held to a
consistent empirical standard. Two, Concern

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.920
for the emotional well-being of students
cannot become a free pass for academic folly.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.280
It's healthy and natural for
parents and teachers to care how

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:53.340
children are doing socially and
emotionally. But, ultimately, schools must

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:58.320
be places of learning. SEL must remain
tightly linked to a focus on how kids

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:04.019
are doing academically. Absent these
considerations, SEL risks becoming more

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:10.100
about adult agendas than about what kids
need. Do you think that school improvement

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:15.040
efforts usually serve the needs of adults
or kids? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.540
Also, let us know what other
topics you'd like our scholars to cover

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:24.800
in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE and
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

